Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:40:54 -0500
Subject: feat: ask a peek's permissions over the page

A page in a peek over the page that asked for a permission got no prompt. The
request manager comes with a tab's features, and a peek is no tab, so nothing took
the request and the page was answered as if a prompt had been ignored. The peek now
makes the manager itself, as the contextual tasks panel does for its page, and the
page keeps it when it becomes a tab.

The prompt hangs from the card's bar, under the site, since a peek has no address
row of its own, and its title names the page's site. It goes and comes with the
peek, whose tab another tab on screen hides. Closing the peek takes it along. Open
as Tab takes the prompt down with the card and keeps the question, and the page
asks it again in its tab, as a tab asks.

Why: peek P20 (BACKLOG S-376). A permission asked for in a peek was lost, and the
page's only way to get one was Open as Tab and asking again.
Removable when: the peek over the page leaves the series.
